---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' }).format(
  new Date()
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What data TravelHackz collects, what it doesn't, and how the site's embeds, analytics and newsletter work."
>
  <section class="container page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="lead">
      TravelHackz is a small, independent travel blog. This page explains, in plain language,
      what data touches this site and why.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel Web Analytics</a>
      to understand which posts get read and roughly how many people visit. It's cookieless and doesn't
      track you individually across other websites — it only reports aggregate numbers like page views
      and referrers.
    </p>

    <h2>Embedded Players</h2>
    <p>
      Podcast episodes on this site are embedded directly from Spotify and Apple Podcasts. When you
      interact with one of those players, Spotify or Apple may set their own cookies or collect data
      according to their own privacy policies — that's outside our control. We only load the player
      when you visit a page that has one; we don't add any tracking of our own on top of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      If you subscribe to our newsletter, your email address is stored with our email provider,
      <a href="https://buttondown.email" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buttondown</a>, solely to send
      you new posts and updates. We don't sell or share your email with anyone else. You can
      unsubscribe at any time using the link in any email we send.
    </p>

    <h2>Partner Links</h2>
    <p>
      Some posts link to <a href="https://www.keepsmybag.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Keepsmybag</a>,
      a luggage delivery service we mention because we think it's genuinely useful for travelers to
      Istanbul. Clicking through takes you to their site, which has its own separate privacy policy —
      we don't receive any personal data about what you do there.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Don't Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't require an account or login to read the site.</li>
      <li>We don't process payments or store financial information — TravelHackz doesn't sell anything directly.</li>
      <li>We don't sell, rent, or share your data with advertisers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email us at
      <a href={`mailto:info.travelhackz@gmail.com`}>info.travelhackz@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: -0.5rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
